    "chapter_name": "Chemical Kinetics",
    "year": "2023",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A and B are two substances undergoing radioactive decay in a container. The half life of A&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math> and that of B is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>. If the initial concentration of B is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> times that of A and they both start decaying at the same time, how much time will it take for the concentration of both of them to be same? ________min."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For a first order reaction:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>kt</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> : Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be x<br />For a first order reaction:<br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>xe</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>kt</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>xe</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; ....(1)</p><p>Similarly For B:<br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>kt</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>xe</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ....(2)<br />Equating equation(1) and (2) we get:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>xe</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>xe</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math></p>"
  }
}